        "parms": "# array — a named list of values\narray notes holds an ordered list of elements, each one value: an int, a float or a word. It opens holding 60 64 67 72, because the contents are saved with the patch. Positions start at 0, and a position the array does not have is refused, never wrapped.\nEvery .array object takes the name of its array as the first argument, and objects with the same name share one array. Unlike Max, an array never travels down a cord: a cord carries only the reference array notes, and any .array object it reaches runs on that array. For now, place the .array before the other objects that name its array: when one of them was placed first, the saved contents do not load (yse-soundengine#1245).",
